WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.779 --> 00:00:02.328
- [Narrator] In Japan, restaurants,

00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:05.400
and to be clear, I mean
a ton of restaurants,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.233
use plastic food displays
to entice customers.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.046
And in Gujo province,
there's a small factory

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.465
that's responsible for more than half

00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:17.135
of all the plastic sushi, crab,

00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:18.708
omelets, duck, ramen, beef,

00:00:18.708 --> 00:00:21.208
oh my God, that's all plastic?

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:24.756
This is Satori Kaboki.

00:00:24.756 --> 00:00:28.589
- (speaking foreign language)

00:00:31.045 --> 00:00:33.016
- [Narrator] This factory has
about 30 full-time artists

00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:37.107
because all these plastic
foods are made by hand.

00:00:37.107 --> 00:00:41.274
- [Takahiro] (speaks in foreign language)

00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:53.737
- [Narrator] Takahiro is an artist here.

00:00:53.737 --> 00:00:57.904
- [Takahiro] (speaks in foreign language)

00:01:06.293 --> 00:01:10.210
- (speaks in foreign language)

00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:14.680
- [Narrator] This trend
of plastic food in Japan

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.852
has been around since the
1930s, but blew up in the ‘50s.

00:01:18.852 --> 00:01:21.220
And it is everywhere.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.602
However, this food, it doesn't come cheap.

00:01:24.602 --> 00:01:28.519
- (speaks in foreign language)

00:01:36.922 --> 00:01:39.311
- [Narrator] It takes years of
training to master this art.

00:01:39.311 --> 00:01:43.478
- [Takahiro] (speaking
in foreign language)

00:01:45.292 --> 00:01:46.711
- [Narrator] Quick example:

00:01:46.711 --> 00:01:49.092
A bowl of ramen might
take three hours to make,

00:01:49.092 --> 00:01:52.292
while a fish: many, many more.

00:01:52.292 --> 00:01:56.459
- [Takahiro] (speaking
